id: pm-9url9h
title: "Dispatch daily releases at 04:45 Europe/Vienna with the hosted schedule as fallback"
description: "Add an independently timed workflow dispatch for early-morning release preparation while retaining the existing GitHub schedule, UTC-day version identity, hosted publication gates and immutable-tag recovery. Target completion before 06:30-07:00 local time without claiming a guarantee under offline hosts or failed release gates."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[2]: "area:release",automation
created_at: "2026-09-26T07:47:55.227Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-26T08:25:19.772Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-26T08:25:19.031Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-26T08:25:19.031Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: "A DST-aware timer fires at 04:45 Europe/Vienna;The dispatcher targets main with explicit production inputs and refuses overlapping or duplicate daily dispatches;The hosted cron and its historical reliability denominator remain unchanged;Dry-run and negative controls prove no publication during setup verification;Operator documentation explains timing limitations and rollback"
parent: pm-u9d0
resolution: "Implemented and documented a DST-aware independent morning dispatcher, preserving native fallback and hosted release gates, with exact-tag and active-run checks, exclusive daily intent, read-only checks and actual CLI failure-path coverage."
expected_result: "An independently timed 04:45 Vienna request reaches the existing gated production workflow without duplicate requests, unsafe late catch-up or altered native reliability accounting."
actual_result: "58 linked tests, 37 isolated rechecks, full local static quality, typecheck, docs and history checks passed. The dispatcher has 100% focused statement/branch/function/line coverage. Protected unattended service authentication and both DST calendars passed. Private units are staged disabled for activation after reviewed merge; future publication timing remains an operational target, not a guaranteed result."
