comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-26T07:47:55.227Z","harness:codex","text=Duplicate checks: context plus open/in_progress listings and keyword searches for release schedule, dispatch, reliability and morning. Existing timing and reliability work delivered measurement rather than an external clock. Live run 36111244838 was created 08:07:47Z and its job started 08:07:51Z against cron 02:35Z. The release environment has branch policy only and no wait timer."
  "2026-09-26T07:50:59.505Z","harness:codex","Decision: user approved a local systemd timer plus the unchanged GitHub fallback. Primary target 04:45 Europe/Vienna with one 05:00 retry opportunity for failures before dispatch. Native cron stays 02:35 UTC and reliability-policy values remain unchanged, preserving historical attribution. External dispatches stay outside the native scheduled denominator. Service checks active release workflows and exact UTC-day tags; an exclusive daily intent marker precedes the POST so uncertain acceptance cannot cause an automatic repeat. No publish or workflow dispatch is performed during setup checks."
  "2026-09-26T07:52:35.437Z","harness:codex","Verification: all 53 linked tests pass (21 dispatcher, 8 native reliability, 24 release automation contracts). systemd-analyze validates the private units and confirms 04:45 CEST on September 27 and 04:45 CET after the October 25 transition. An unattended read-only transient user service, with the same protected filesystem and existing keyring authentication as production, completed in 2.7 seconds and reported would_dispatch. It created no intent and sent no workflow dispatch. User linger was already enabled. Timer activation remains deferred until reviewed delivery."
  "2026-09-26T08:02:31.809Z","harness:codex","Additional verification: pnpm typecheck and docs-skills gate passed. pm validate --check-resolution --check-history-drift reports ok=true with 170 pre-existing missing-resolution warnings; the new task history hash verifies. A broad local coverage run was interrupted after unrelated expensive tests failed under concurrent validation load; it is not coverage proof. The affected files are being rerun with one worker and hosted full coverage remains mandatory before merge."
  "2026-09-26T08:04:27.483Z","harness:codex","Contention follow-up: all 37 tests in the five affected files pass with one worker (181.53 seconds): merge-receipt-health-classification, operation-source-contract, absence-tolerance-gate, aggregate-set-members and refusal-closure-gate. No unrelated production or test code was changed. The interrupted full coverage run remains explicitly unproved; CI must supply full coverage evidence."
  "2026-09-26T08:11:28.443Z","harness:codex","Final local static evidence: pnpm quality:static completed successfully, including lint, zero-duplicate scans, workflow policy checks, generated-contract checks, repository static quality, package/public-surface checks, tracker governance and bounded mutation controls (323 killed, 7 equivalent, 330 total). No native workflow or reliability-policy file changed. The reviewed delivery includes the generated changelog."
  "2026-09-26T08:25:18.187Z","harness:codex","Hosted review follow-up: the first PR head passed all functional tests but exact coverage identified the new script CLI entrypoint and malformed census branches. Added actual-entrypoint success/error tests and malformed API negative controls without changing production code or coverage policy. All 58 linked release tests pass. Focused dispatcher coverage is 56/56 statements, 45/45 branches, 9/9 functions and 42/42 lines. Focused lint and zero-duplicate checks pass. First-head CodeFactor and DeepScan report zero issues; final-head hosted checks remain required. Sourcery reported quota exhaustion; CodeRabbit review was explicitly requested through the reviewer API."
